ous existence  in their response to suffering they have  thrashed so hard trying to escape it  they have seemed to repeatedly and  increasingly damage themselves  i'm scared of what this means for me  i'm scared that because of this i will  experience or become a part of further  malevolence and self-damage and worse i  will understand it i will know why there  is evil and i might even if by accident  become it  what are you impressed by and happy  about  in a way what i am impressed by is  similar to what i am scared of and  concerned about that the human project  has survived this long without complete  self-destruction intentional or  accidental that it has been able to  complete and build entire structures and  systems of function physical  organizational and cultural and that it  has been able to create grand illusions  so robust and so powerful that it can  persuade itself enough individually and  collectively that there is reason to  continue  although deeply challenged and imperfect  humanity has charged forward and  seemingly created a world for itself for  better or for worse there is no doubting  the impressiveness  despite their great conflicts they have  in many ways truly come together  humanity is so compelled by its own  ignorance it has become an almost  courage  over the last day i've scanned nearly  every movie about ancient eras of their  history and in many of them there seems  to be an important scene where a  protagonist runs head-on into a battle  or situation where the odds of success  are basically zero i calculated the odds  each time using simulation models  however in each of these scenes somehow  the ignorance seems to almost morph into  valor  perhaps the movie of humanity as a whole  is like this then as it charges  individually and collectively forward at  the outmatching ranks of the universe  its odds are essentially zero but yet it  continues anyway  and i think for some reason that  embodies the word beautiful for me  write what 